{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1486","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1486","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1486\",\"parent_revision\":\"17996f08959076907ab74a35c87a4f5fa021c6ba\",\"root_revision\":\"7a461bc1a4e1c47822c0a327bdb494e9d54ec0a3e7e0f28a25a86a90ebdb5cfd\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: groomed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe backlog_view tool has a sections= parameter that lets callers request only specific sections of an item, avoiding the cost of loading full item bodies. The grooming skill (and related skills calling backlog_view) do not use this parameter \u2014 they fetch complete item bodies even when only a subset of sections is needed. This wastes context window budget on every grooming invocation.\\n\\nEvidence: backlog MCP server backlog_view tool definition (sections= parameter confirmed present); skills/grooming skill files confirmed to call backlog_view without sections= argument.\\n\\nVerbatim user report: \\\"group these into combined tasks that can be done via the /python-tdd process\\\"\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **grooming skill ignores backlog_view sections= parameter, fetching full item bodies unnecessarily** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research finding \u2014 mcp-ux-improvements-20260404.md, validated mcp-ux-improvements-validation-20260404.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7dd63157b5174fa4a2ed1b206879a1e9de351cff5dcb209ef0751fe0d8787620\",\"comment_id\":\"IC